🎟️ Mini-Project: "The Nightclub API"
Objective: Build a backend system that strictly controls who enters the club based on specific rules (Age, Capacity, and VIP status).
1. The Data (Entity)
I need a database table called Guest with these columns:
 * id (Auto-generated)
 * name (String)
 * age (Integer)
 * isVip (Boolean) - Default this to false.
2. The API Endpoint (The Door)
Create one endpoint: POST /club/enter
 * Input Body: A JSON object with name and age.
 * Input Header: A custom header named X-VIP-PASS (Optional).
3. The Business Rules (Service Layer)
Your Service must enforce these 3 strict rules before saving to the database:
 * The ID Check: If the guest is under 21, they are rejected immediately.
 * The VIP Check: If the X-VIP-PASS header contains the exact password "GOLD-ACCESS", the guest is marked as a VIP (isVip = true).
 * The Capacity Check: The club is tiny. It only holds 5 people.
   * If there are already 5 people in the database, Normal guests are rejected.
   * VIPs ignore the capacity limit (they can always enter, even if there are 100 people).
4. The Responses (Controller Layer)
You must handle the rejections using Local Exception Handling (try-catch) and return the correct HTTP Status Codes:
| Scenario | HTTP Status | Response Body (Message) |
|---|---|---|
| Success | 201 Created | The saved Guest object |
| Under 21 | 400 Bad Request | "Underage entry denied." |
| Club Full (Normal Guest) | 503 Service Unavailable | "Club is full." |
🧪 Your Testing Checklist (Postman)
Once you finish coding, you must pass these 4 tests to consider the project "Done".
 * The Kid Test: Try to add a 17-year-old. -> Must fail (400).
 * The Crowd Test: Add 5 adults (age 25) successfully. -> Must get 201 for all.
 * The Rejection Test: Try to add a 6th adult without a header. -> Must fail (503).
 * The VIP Test: Try to add a 7th adult WITH the header X-VIP-PASS: GOLD-ACCESS. -> Must succeed (201).
